-- Income 220, above the appropriate minimum guarantee by 20: the guarantee credit condition fails (220 > 200),
-- so no guarantee credit. Savings: qualifying income 220 > 150; A = smaller of 30 and 50% of 70 = 35, so 30;
-- B = 50% of the excess 20 = 10; A exceeds B: savings credit 30 - 10 = 20. She is entitled to state pension
-- credit through the savings route (s 1(2)(c)(ii)). Total 0 + 20 = 20.
