§§ `Couples (sections 3(1)(b), 3ZA, 4(1), 4(1A), 5, 17(1))`
-- Margaret is married to Harold and they share a household: a couple (s 17(1) "couple", limb (a)).
-- Margaret has 100 a week of retirement pension income, Harold 120; qualifying income 100 and 120.
-- Aggregation (s 5): income 220, qualifying income 220. The standard minimum guarantee for a member of a
-- couple is 300; no additions: 300. Guarantee credit 300 - 220 = 80. Savings credit: Margaret's pensionable age
-- (2010) is before 6 April 2016 and she is over 65 (s 3(1)(a)); qualifying income 220 > 150; maximum savings
-- credit 60% of (300 - 150) = 90; A = smaller of 90 and 50% of 70 = 35; B = 0 (220 <= 300); savings credit 35.
-- Total 80 + 35 = 115. Harold's pensionable age (2014) and qualifying age (2009) are before 6 April 2016 too, so
-- they are not a mixed-age couple (s 3ZA(3)).
#ASSERT `whether I am a member of a couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `the income that counts as mine` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 0 0 100 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 120 0 0 0 0 0 0 0 FALSE EQUALS 220
