-- "Couple" (s 17(1)) in the four ways it can arise. Limb (a): married or civil partners AND the same household.
-- Limb (b): NOT married or civil partners, but living together as if they were, otherwise than in prescribed
-- circumstances. Married but in different households: not a couple (a). Not married, not living together as
-- if married: not a couple. Not married, living together as if married, but within the regulations'
-- exception: not a couple.
#ASSERT `whether I am a member of a couple` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `whether I am a member of a couple` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`whether I am a member of a couple` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`whether I am a member of a couple` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`whether I am a member of a couple` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

