§§ `6 Duty to specify assessed income period for pre-6 April 2016 awards`
-- Margaret (65 on 10 May 2015), single, decision taking effect 1 June 2015: the Secretary of State determined
-- her income (s 6(3)(a)), under section 8(1), 9 or 10 of the Social Security Act 1998 (b), on or after her 65th
-- birthday (c), and not a refusal (d): the first case; before 6 April 2016, so he MUST specify a period (s 6(1)).
-- If he considers her particulars not likely to be typical of the next 12 months (s 9(2)) he NEED NOT specify one,
-- and one he does specify must be shorter than 5 years.
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `The Secretary of State need not specify an assessed income period, and any period specified must be shorter than 5 years`
-- The boundary days. 9 May 2015 (the day before her 65th birthday): not within the cases. 10 May 2015: within.
-- 5 April 2016 (before 6 April 2016): the section applies. 6 April 2016: it does not.
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 5 9) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Section 6 does not apply to the decision`
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 5 10) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2016 4 5) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2016 4 6) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Section 6 does not apply to the decision`
-- A decision to the effect that she is NOT entitled is not in the first case (s 6(3)(d)).
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Section 6 does not apply to the decision`
-- The second case (s 6(4)): her income was determined on an appeal against a refusal, and on the appeal she was
-- found entitled; the decision takes effect as in s 6(3)(c). The Secretary of State must specify a period.
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
-- Prevented (s 6(2)): a period is already in force from an earlier application of section 6, or other prescribed
-- circumstances prevent it.
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State is prevented from specifying an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State is prevented from specifying an assessed income period`
-- A couple (s 6(3)(c)(ii)): Tom is not yet 65 on 1 June 2015 (he is 65 on 1 January 2023) but his partner Margaret
-- was 65 on 10 May 2015, so the day the other member attains 65 governs if earlier: the section applies. Tom living
-- alone does not get that: the decision is before his own 65th birthday.
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Man (YearMonthDay 1958 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 1 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `The Secretary of State must specify an assessed income period`
#ASSERT `what section 6 requires of the Secretary of State for me` Man (YearMonthDay 1958 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2023 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `Section 6 does not apply to the decision`

§§ `7 Fixing of claimant's retirement provision for assessed income period`
-- What counts as retirement provision (s 7(6)): retirement pension income other than benefit under Part 1 of the
-- Pensions Act 2014 or the Contributions and Benefits Act; income from annuity contracts other than retirement pension
-- income; income from capital; PPF periodic payments. A Category A or B retirement pension is excluded. A
-- Northern Ireland benefit of the same kind is not on the literal wording (fork F-12). A private pension is in.
-- Earnings are not. A payment by a former employer on early retirement is retirement pension income (s 16(1)(l)) unless
-- a court ordered it or it settled a claim.
#ASSERT NOT (`whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `a Category A or Category B retirement pension` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `a Category A or Category B retirement pension` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `income from an occupational pension scheme or a personal pension scheme` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `income from capital` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `PPF periodic payments` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `income from an annuity contract other than retirement pension income` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `earnings` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`whether this income is part of my retirement provision` `a payment by a former employer on account of early retirement on grounds of ill-health or disability` TRUE FALSE)

-- The amount of an element during the period (s 7(3) to (5)): the assessed amount (100) varied by the prescribed
-- changes. An increase counts (+10 on 1 April 2021: 110 from that day, 100 the day before). A decrease counts only for
-- income from capital (s 7(4)(b)): -7 on 1 June 2022 takes an income-from-capital element from 100 to 93 but leaves
-- any other element at 100. An element the relevant decision did not count (s 7(5)) is taken not to be there: 0.
-- Prescribed circumstances in which the amount is not deemed to vary: it stays 100. No prescribed change: 100.
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2021 3 31) 100 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 10 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 100 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 10 EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) 100 FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) (-7) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 31) 100 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) (-7) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) 100 TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1) (-7) EQUALS 93
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 100 FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 10 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 100 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 10 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the amount of this income counted on the day` (YearMonthDay 2021 4 1) 100 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) 0 EQUALS 100

§§ `8 Fresh determinations increasing claimant's entitlement`
-- May fresh determinations be made (s 8(1), (2))? (a) for a decision under section 10 of the 1998 Act; (b) the new
-- decision increases the amount (100 to 120); (c) the increase results at least in part from them. Yes. Not if it is
-- not a section 10 decision. Not if the amount does not increase (100 to 100) and does not reduce.
-- A reduction deemed to satisfy (b) and (c) if it is less than it would have been without them (s 8(2)):
-- 100 to 90 where it would have been 100 to 80: yes; 100 to 90 where it would have been 90 too: no.
#ASSERT `whether fresh determinations of my retirement provision may be made` TRUE TRUE 100 120 110
#ASSERT NOT (`whether fresh determinations of my retirement provision may be made` FALSE TRUE 100 120 110)
#ASSERT NOT (`whether fresh determinations of my retirement provision may be made` TRUE TRUE 100 100 90)
#ASSERT `whether fresh determinations of my retirement provision may be made` TRUE FALSE 100 90 80
#ASSERT NOT (`whether fresh determinations of my retirement provision may be made` TRUE FALSE 100 90 90)
-- Which determination governs (s 8(3)): from the day the new decision takes effect (15 June 2020), including that
-- day, the fresh determination; before it, the one it replaces.
#ASSERT `which determination governs on the day` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 14) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) EQUALS `The determination it replaces governs`
#ASSERT `which determination governs on the day` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) EQUALS `The fresh determination governs`
#ASSERT `which determination governs on the day` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 16) (YearMonthDay 2020 6 15) EQUALS `The fresh determination governs`

§§ `9 Duration of assessed income period`
-- Length (s 9(1)): under 75 on the day the decision takes effect: 5 years; 75 or over: indefinite. Born 1 March 1940,
-- 75 on 1 March 2015: a decision on 28 February 2015 gives 5 years; on 1 March 2015, indefinite. Margaret, born 1950,
-- decision 1 June 2015, is 65: 5 years.
#ASSERT `how long my assessed income period lasts` (YearMonthDay 2015 2 28) (YearMonthDay 1940 3 1) EQUALS `Five years beginning with the day the relevant decision takes effect`
#ASSERT `how long my assessed income period lasts` (YearMonthDay 2015 3 1) (YearMonthDay 1940 3 1) EQUALS `An indefinite period beginning with that day`
#ASSERT `how long my assessed income period lasts` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) EQUALS `Five years beginning with the day the relevant decision takes effect`
-- Margaret, single, period beginning 1 June 2015, under 75: 5 years, so the first day on which it is not in force
-- is 1 June 2020; it is in force on 31 May 2020 and not on 1 June 2020; and not in force on 31 May 2015 (before it began).
-- Nothing in the case ends it earlier: she was 65 before it began.
#ASSERT `the first day my assessed income period is no longer in force` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1)
#ASSERT `whether my assessed income period is in force on the day` (YearMonthDay 2020 5 31) Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`whether my assessed income period is in force on the day` (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1) Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`whether my assessed income period is in force on the day` (YearMonthDay 2015 5 31) Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT `whether my assessed income period is in force on the day` (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE
-- The period ends (s 9(4)) when she becomes or ceases to be a member of a couple: 1 January 2017.
-- It ends at a further time the regulations prescribe (s 9(5)): 9 September 2016 (earlier than the 2017 event, and
-- earlier than the 5 years). Where the regulations prescribe circumstances in which s 9(4) does not apply to her
-- (but not s 9(5)): the couple event of 2017 is disregarded and the 9 September 2016 time governs; with no s 9(5) time
-- the period runs its 5 years to 1 June 2020.
#ASSERT `the first day my assessed income period is no longer in force` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1)
#ASSERT `the first day my assessed income period is no longer in force` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9)
#ASSERT `the first day my assessed income period is no longer in force` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2016 9 9)
#ASSERT `the first day my assessed income period is no longer in force` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2017 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) TRUE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 6 1)
-- The other member of a couple attains 65 (s 9(4)(d)): Margaret is married to Walter, who is 65 on 3 March 2017: the
-- period ends on 3 March 2017.
#ASSERT `the first day my assessed income period is no longer in force` Woman (YearMonthDay 1950 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) (YearMonthDay 2010 5 10) TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE Man (YearMonthDay 1952 3 3) (YearMonthDay 2017 3 3) (YearMonthDay 2012 3 3) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2017 3 3)
-- Gladys, born 1 January 1938, is 75 on 1 January 2013, so a period beginning on 1 June 2015 is indefinite (s 9(1)(b)):
-- no day on which it ends, and it is still in force on 22 October 2026.
#ASSERT `the first day my assessed income period is no longer in force` Woman (YearMonthDay 1938 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `whether my assessed income period is in force on the day` (YearMonthDay 2026 10 22) Woman (YearMonthDay 1938 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1998 1 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE Woman (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 1900 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2015 6 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) FALSE

§§ `10 Effect of variations under section 7(4)`
-- Section 10(2): an assessed income period is in force, an element is varied under section 7(4), and the variation
-- affects the amount: from the commencing date (1 April 2024) the changed amount (60) is paid with no further
-- decision. The day before, the amount she is paid before the change (50) continues (fork F-23). A reduction is
-- the same (40). Where any of the three is missing section 10 does not apply and the encoding gives no amount. Same
-- amount before and after: it continues (s 10(3)).
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 60 EQUALS JUST 50
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 60 EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 60 EQUALS JUST 60
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 40 EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) FALSE TRUE TRUE 50 60 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE 50 60 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE 50 60 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the state pension credit I am paid on the day` (YearMonthDay 2024 4 2) (YearMonthDay 2024 4 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE 50 50 EQUALS JUST 50
-- Does the Secretary of State have to make a further decision before the changed amount is paid? Section 10(2) says
-- not, when section 10 applies; when it does not apply the Act does not say.
#ASSERT `whether a new decision is needed before the changed amount is paid` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `The Act says no`
#ASSERT `whether a new decision is needed before the changed amount is paid` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`
#ASSERT `whether a new decision is needed before the changed amount is paid` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`
#ASSERT `whether a new decision is needed before the changed amount is paid` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`

§§ `Schedules 1 and 2`
-- Schedule 1 paragraph 3(3A): the Administration Act's power to require information or evidence includes evidence
-- of the likelihood of future changes in her circumstances, needed to decide whether to specify an assessed income
-- period (a) or its length (b). Yes if it is such evidence and it is for (a), or for (b), or both; no if it is not that
-- kind of evidence, or is needed for neither.
#ASSERT `whether I can be asked for evidence about likely future changes` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `whether I can be asked for evidence about likely future changes` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `whether I can be asked for evidence about likely future changes` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`whether I can be asked for evidence about likely future changes` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`whether I can be asked for evidence about likely future changes` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- Paragraph 12: an appeal lies against the four decisions about an assessed income period; for any other kind of
-- decision the paragraph does not say (the general law of appeals is outside the encoding).
#ASSERT `whether I can appeal against the decision` `A decision whether to specify a period as an assessed income period under section 6` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `whether I can appeal against the decision` `A decision as to the period to be so specified` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `whether I can appeal against the decision` `A decision whether an assessed income period comes to an end by virtue of section 9(4) or (5)` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `whether I can appeal against the decision` `A decision as to when the assessed income period so ends` EQUALS `The Act says yes`
#ASSERT `whether I can appeal against the decision` `A decision of another kind` EQUALS `Not covered by this encoding`
-- Paragraph 13: for a period of less than a week (6 days) the prescribed amount (12) is paid; 7 days is a week, and the
-- paragraph says nothing (fork F-17). Prescribed nil: 0.
#ASSERT `what I am paid for a period of less than a week` 6 12 EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `what I am paid for a period of less than a week` 6 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `what I am paid for a period of less than a week` 7 12 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `what I am paid for a period of less than a week` 8 12 EQUALS NOTHING
